  "reason": "P0.5-04 integrates the shared adaptive Workbench into practice and review. Pane resize, expansion and narrow region switching preserve mounted Blockly/source/player identities; hidden review playback is paused and keyboard guarded. SAVE2 existing layout fields use generation/revision CAS and explicit sparse retry, and no pending theme preview is submitted by layout changes. Only PracticeExecution changed among the twelve registered sources. After its final edit, the genuine 45 block/practice integrations, 3 named navigation integrations, complete 914 frontend checks and 24 new layout checks passed within 165 unique three-browser scenarios. The first broad run passed163/165; its two Firefox drag failures were caused by off-viewport test coordinates, now using the actual visible splitter midpoint. Captured moves with no held button also cancel safely. After an intermediate23/24 exposed an invalid second mouse click while the first pointer remained held in Firefox, the peer update now uses genuine keyboard controls. The final layout suite independently passed24/24 after that narrow correction; the other141 successful scenarios remain valid and source registration gates are unchanged. C subset, content/learning identities, Rust and runtime budgets are unchanged. Background import P0.5-03 was cancelled by the user; legacy SAVE2 fields remain compatible.",
